# Members of lib/zinc.d.ts that the engine does not provide yet, with the reason. tools/dts-walk skips them.
Console.table needs the object formatter of the dyn prelude for rows and columns; tracked with the Node console parity items
Promise.catch the declaration is an overload pair, the probe picks the wrong signature (Promise.catch itself works)
String.replaceAll the probe has no RegExp in its program, so the regular expression prelude is absent; covered by tests/golden/run/regexp_corpus.ts
String.split the probe has no RegExp in its program, so the regular expression prelude is absent; covered by tests/golden/run/regexp_corpus.ts
String.match the probe has no RegExp in its program, so the regular expression prelude is absent; covered by tests/golden/run/regexp_corpus.ts
String.matchAll the probe has no RegExp in its program, so the regular expression prelude is absent; covered by tests/golden/run/regexp_corpus.ts
String.search the probe has no RegExp in its program, so the regular expression prelude is absent; covered by tests/golden/run/regexp_corpus.ts
String.replace the declaration is an overload pair (string or RegExp), the probe picks the wrong signature; covered by tests/golden/run/regexp_corpus.ts
StringConstructor.raw only as a tag (String.raw`...`, rewritten by the parser), never called with an array
Array.push the probe calls it with no argument (the rest parameter); one value or one spread `push(...b)` is what the engine takes (ZN-160)
